{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "edunest-api-collection-v1",
		"name": "EduNest API — Auth + Super-Admin + Provision (Phase 4)",
		"description": "# EduNest API — Manual Testing Collection\n\nCovers **all currently implemented routes** (`backend/src/app.ts`):\n\n- `GET /api/health`\n- `POST /api/auth/admin-request`, `/api/auth/login`, `/api/auth/refresh`, `/api/auth/logout`, `GET /api/auth/me`\n- `GET /api/super/requests`, `POST /api/super/requests/:id/approve`, `POST /api/super/requests/:id/reject`\n- `POST /api/super/institutes`, `GET /api/super/institutes`, `GET /api/super/institutes/:id`, `PATCH /api/super/institutes/:id/status`\n\n> NOTE: Admin / Teacher / Student / Classes / Timetable / Attendance / Tests / Fees / Salary / Notices / Complaints / Reports routes from `backendplan.md` are **NOT implemented yet** — so they are intentionally NOT in this collection.\n\n## Setup (2 min)\n\n1. Start backend: `cd backend` then `npm run dev` (expects `PORT=4000`, MongoDB running, `backend/.env` filled — see `backend/.env.example`).\n2. Import this file into Postman: **Import → File → EduNest.postman_collection.json**.\n3. Select collection → **Variables** tab → set:\n   - `baseUrl` = `http://localhost:4000/api`\n   - `superEmail` = your `SUPER_EMAIL` from `backend/.env` (default in `.env.example` is `super@edunest.in`)\n   - `superPassword` = your `SUPER_PASSWORD` (default in `.env.example` is `Super@123`)\n4. Cookies: Postman saves `edunest_token` + `edunest_refresh` (httpOnly) automatically. Keep **Cookie Jar enabled** (Postman does this by default). Login once, then all `Super` + `Me` requests work.\n5. Follow the **suggested order** below (folder order = workflow order).\n\n## Suggested manual flow\n\n1. `Health` → should be `{ ok: true, data: { service, db, time } }`.\n2. `Auth / 01 + 02 Admin Request` → creates 2 pending schools. Test scripts auto-save `instituteId` and `rejectInstituteId`.\n3. `Auth / 04 Login Super-Admin` → sets cookies (also returns `{ user }`).\n4. `Super Requests / List Pending` → see your 2 new rows, copy `instituteId` if needed.\n5. `Super Requests / Approve` → approves `{{instituteId}}`.\n6. `Super Institutes / Direct Create` → offline onboarding, auto-saves new `{{instituteId}}` + `tempPassword` (returned ONCE).\n7. `Super Institutes / Directory + Detail + Status` → block/unblock/suspend/unsuspend cycle.\n8. `Auth / Me, Refresh, Logout` → session checks.\n\nAll success bodies use envelope `{ ok: true, data: ... }`. Errors use `{ ok: false, error, details? }` with `400/401/403/404/409/429`.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"variable": [
